89	## Link Styling
90	
91	**Never rely on browser default link colors.** The default blue (`#0000EE`) has poor contrast on dark backgrounds. Style links with `color: var(--accent)` and keep underlines for discoverability. On dark backgrounds, use bright accents (`#22d3ee`, `#34d399`, `#fbbf24`). On light backgrounds, use deeper tones (`#0891b2`, `#059669`, `#d97706`).
92	
93	## Section / Card Components
94	
95	The fundamental building block. A colored card representing a system component, pipeline step, or data entity.
96	
97	**IMPORTANT: Never use `.node` as a CSS class name.** Mermaid.js internally uses `.node` on its SVG `<g>` elements with `transform: translate(x, y)` for positioning. Any page-level `.node` styles (hover transforms, box-shadows, transitions) will leak into Mermaid diagrams and break their layout. Use `.ve-card` instead (namespaced to avoid collisions with CSS frameworks like Bootstrap/Tailwind that also use `.card`).
98	
99	```css
100	.ve-card {
101	  background: var(--surface);
102	  border: 1px solid var(--border);
103	  border-radius: 10px;
104	  padding: 16px 20px;
105	  position: relative;
106	}
107	
108	/* Colored accent border (left or top) */
109	.ve-card--accent-a {
110	  border-left: 3px solid var(--node-a);
111	}
112	
113	/* --- Depth tiers: vary card depth to signal importance --- */
114	
115	/* Elevated: KPIs, key sections, anything that should pop */
116	.ve-card--elevated {
117	  background: var(--surface-elevated);
118	  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08), 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
119	}
120	
121	/* Recessed: code blocks, secondary content, detail panels */
122	.ve-card--recessed {
123	  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 70%, var(--surface) 30%);
124	  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
125	  border-color: var(--border);
126	}
127	
128	/* Hero: executive summaries, focal elements — demands attention */
129	.ve-card--hero {
130	  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 92%, var(--accent) 8%);
131	  box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08), 0 1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
132	  border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--border) 50%, var(--accent) 50%);
133	}
134	
135	/* Glass: special-occasion overlay effect (use sparingly) */
136	.ve-card--glass {
137	  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 60%, transparent 40%);
138	  backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
139	  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
140	  border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
141	}
142	
143	/* Section label (monospace, uppercase, small) */
144	.ve-card__label {
145	  font-family: var(--font-mono);
146	  font-size: 10px;
147	  font-weight: 600;
148	  text-transform: uppercase;
149	  letter-spacing: 1.5px;
150	  color: var(--node-a);
151	  margin-bottom: 10px;
152	  display: flex;
153	  align-items: center;
154	  gap: 8px;
155	}
156	
157	/* Colored dot indicator */
158	.ve-card__label::before {
159	  content: '';
160	  width: 8px;
161	  height: 8px;
162	  border-radius: 50%;
163	  background: currentColor;
164	}
165	```
